{"kind":"request","text":"Design note: dap-family, a family tree, genealogy record and history map on dap.\n\nFiled 2026-11-23 at Hugh's request. Hugh asked for an overall design of a new application, dap-family, with these requirements: a model of people, relationships, major life events, locations and references to external sources; the map view of dap-foldkit; several participants; a member can claim a person record as \"this is me\"; invitations bound to an existing person record and unbound invitations, after which the invitee creates their own record; anonymous viewers; and a design that can scale to everyone.\n\nThe draft design is in ~/play/dap-family/DESIGN.md, with UI sketches in ~/play/dap-family/sketches/index.html. This request moves the design into a dated note in notes/, with every dap fact read again at main b0a6439a, and asks for an independent review.\n\nThe note proposes:\n1. One scope for each person, couple, place and source. A circle is a room with membership and invitations.\n2. No fan-in on the write path. A parentage lives in the child's scope, and a couple has its own scope. Citations and events name a source or a place by ID and send it nothing.\n3. A claim is an item in the person scope. A bound invitation offers the claim to that scope, and the invitee redeems it with the invitation's secret.\n4. Anonymous readers read a public projection that is published from the fold. No anonymous reader reads a scope.\n5. Reads at scale go through an index that can be rebuilt from the record. The browser folds a replica only of the records it writes.\n6. A list of what dap lacks (G1 to G11) and an order of work (F0 to F7).\n\nThe note asks dap for no change. Each gap it names is a candidate request for the planner to file after Hugh's ruling.","body":{"conditions":"A dated design note in notes/ with a status line, every dap fact read at main b0a6439a, under the 40,960-byte note limit. An independent exact-head review by the checker with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Hugh rules on the open questions. The note adds no scope kind, definition name, capability or tool family to dap.","target_head":"b0a6439a343972f8809af8a925984289a421edc2","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}